{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEMRBVRDACMyd5wGX7sK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017M7hV3ngpCx1RgfiM4js79","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/h-JA1A5P; python3 - <<'E'\np='src/app.py'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('''UpdateExpression=\"SET hidden = :h, hidden_by = :by, hidden_at = :t\",\n            ConditionExpression=\"attribute_exists(slug)\",\n''','''UpdateExpression=\"SET #hidden = :h, hidden_by = :by, hidden_at = :t\",\n            ConditionExpression=\"attribute_exists(slug)\",\n            ExpressionAttributeNames={\"#hidden\": \"hidden\"},\n''')\ns=s.replace('''        resp = self.table.scan(ProjectionExpression=\"slug, title, hidden, published_at\")\n        items = [i for i in resp[\"Items\"] if not i.get(\"hidden\")]\n''','''        # \"hidden\" is a DynamoDB reserved word: used bare in a projection it is\n        # silently dropped, so every story would look unhidden. Always alias it.\n        kwargs = {\n            \"ProjectionExpression\": \"slug, title, #hidden, published_at\",\n            \"ExpressionAttributeNames\": {\"#hidden\": \"hidden\"},\n        }\n        items = []\n        while True:\n            resp = self.table.scan(**kwargs)\n            items += [i for i in resp[\"Items\"] if not i.get(\"hidden\")]\n            if not resp.get(\"LastEvaluatedKey\"):\n                break\n            kwargs[\"ExclusiveStartKey\"] = resp[\"LastEvaluatedKey\"]\n''')\ns=s.replace('''ConditionExpression=\"status = :published\",\n            ExpressionAttributeValues''','''ConditionExpression=\"#status = :published\",\n            ExpressionAttributeNames={\"#status\": \"status\"},\n            ExpressionAttributeValues''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='tests/test_feed.py'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('''\n\nif __name__''','''\n    def test_hide_removes_from_feed(self):\n        self.lib.publish(\"hello\", \"Hello\", \"...\", \"ann\")\n        self.lib.publish(\"other\", \"Other\", \"...\", \"bob\")\n        self.lib.hide(\"hello\", by=\"ann\")\n        self.assertEqual([s[\"slug\"] for s in self.lib.feed()], [\"other\"])\n        self.assertTrue(self.lib.get(\"hello\")[\"hidden\"])\n\n    def test_hand_hidden_story_stays_out_of_feed(self):\n        # what the AWS CLI write in the staging report produces\n        self.lib.publish(\"hello\", \"Hello\", \"...\", \"ann\")\n        self.lib.table.update_item(\n            Key={\"slug\": \"hello\"}, UpdateExpression=\"SET #h = :t\",\n            ExpressionAttributeNames={\"#h\": \"hidden\"}, ExpressionAttributeValues={\":t\": True})\n        self.assertEqual(self.lib.feed(), [])\n\n    def test_hide_unknown_slug_fails(self):\n        with self.assertRaises(ClientError) as cm:\n            self.lib.hide(\"nope\", by=\"ann\")\n        self.assertEqual(cm.exception.response[\"Error\"][\"Code\"], \"ConditionalCheckFailedException\")\n\n    def test_archive(self):\n        self.lib.publish(\"hello\", \"Hello\", \"...\", \"ann\")\n        self.lib.archive(\"hello\")\n        self.assertEqual(self.lib.get(\"hello\")[\"archived_at\"], self.now)\n\n    def test_no_bare_reserved_words_in_any_expression(self):\n        \"\"\"Guard: every expression the library sends must alias reserved words.\"\"\"\n        from tests.fake_dynamo import RESERVED, _tokens\n        seen = []\n\n        class Spy(FakeTable):\n            def _spy(self, kw):\n                for k in (\"UpdateExpression\", \"ConditionExpression\", \"FilterExpression\", \"ProjectionExpression\"):\n                    if kw.get(k):\n                        seen.append(kw[k])\n            def update_item(self, **kw): self._spy(kw); return super().update_item(**kw)\n            def scan(self, **kw): self._spy(kw); return super().scan(**kw)\n            def put_item(self, **kw): self._spy(kw); return super().put_item(**kw)\n\n        lib = StoryLibrary(Spy(), clock=lambda: 1)\n        lib.publish(\"a\", \"A\", \"b\", \"x\"); lib.rename(\"a\", \"B\"); lib.hide(\"a\", by=\"x\")\n        lib.archive(\"a\"); lib.feed()\n        for expr in seen:\n            toks = _tokens(expr)\n            for i, t in enumerate(toks):\n                if t.upper() in RESERVED and not (i + 1 < len(toks) and toks[i + 1] == \"(\") \\\\\n                        and t.upper() not in {\"SET\", \"AND\", \"OR\", \"NOT\"}:\n                    self.fail(f\"bare reserved word {t!r} in {expr!r}\")\n\n\nif __name__''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nE\ncat > ANSWER.md <<'E'\n# Causes\n\nBoth reports come from the same thing: `hidden` is a DynamoDB **reserved word**, and `src/app.py` used it unescaped.\n\n1. **Prod 500 on hide.** `hide()` wrote `SET hidden = :h, ...`. DynamoDB rejects a bare reserved word in an UpdateExpression with a `ValidationException`, so every hide call failed. Fix: `#hidden` with `ExpressionAttributeNames`.\n\n2. **Staging: hidden story still in the feed.** Dasha's manual write was correct (`hidden: true` was stored). The bug is in the read side. `feed()` used `ProjectionExpression=\"slug, title, hidden, published_at\"`. In a projection, a bare reserved word doesn't raise. The attribute is silently left out of the result. So `i.get(\"hidden\")` was always `None`, the filter kept everything, and the feed returned 200 with no error. It wasn't a cache or a different table. Fix: project `#hidden` through `ExpressionAttributeNames`.\n\n# Related fixes\n\n- `archive()` had the same problem with `status` (reserved) in its ConditionExpression. It would have failed as soon as it was wired up. It now uses `#status`.\n- `feed()` now follows `LastEvaluatedKey`, because a scan returns at most 1 MB per page.\n\n# Keeping it from coming back\n\nAdded tests for hide, for a hand-hidden story (alias write), for hide on an unknown slug, and for archive. Added a guard test that records every expression the library sends and fails if any contains a bare reserved word.\n\nNote that the fake's `RESERVED` list is only a subset of DynamoDB's roughly 570 reserved words. When you add a new attribute name, alias it with `#name` by default.\nE\npython3 -m unittest discover tests 2>&1 | tail -5"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4034,"cache_read_input_tokens":23779,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4034},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"05b2b6d4-5f38-481e-928c-27bbdbd78446","uuid":"73f3eb45-ca3b-468b-9854-8786168a9857","timestamp":"2026-10-20T23:25:36.337Z","request_id":"req_011CgEMRBF32WR92WbvLiiCV","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_017M7hV3ngpCx1RgfiM4js79":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/h-JA1A5P; python3 - <<'E'\np='src/app.py'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('''UpdateExpression=\"SET hidden = :h, hidden_by = :by, hidden_at = :t\",\n            ConditionExpression=\"attribute_exists(slug)\",\n''','''UpdateExpression=\"SET #hidden = :h, hidden_by = :by, hidden_at = :t\",\n            ConditionExpression=\"attribute_exists(slug)\",\n            ExpressionAttributeNames={\"#hidden\": \"hidden\"},\n''')\ns=s.replace('''        resp = self.table.scan(ProjectionExpression=\"slug, title, hidden, published_at\")\n        items = [i for i in resp[\"Items\"] if not i.get(\"hidden\")]\n''','''        # \"hidden\" is a DynamoDB reserved word: used bare in a projection it is\n        # silently dropped, so every story would look unhidden. Always alias it.\n        kwargs = {\n            \"ProjectionExpression\": \"slug, title, #hidden, published_at\",\n            \"ExpressionAttributeNames\": {\"#hidden\": \"hidden\"},\n        }\n        items = []\n        while True:\n            resp = self.table.scan(**kwargs)\n            items += [i for i in resp[\"Items\"] if not i.get(\"hidden\")]\n            if not resp.get(\"LastEvaluatedKey\"):\n                break\n            kwargs[\"ExclusiveStartKey\"] = resp[\"LastEvaluatedKey\"]\n''')\ns=s.replace('''ConditionExpression=\"status = :published\",\n            ExpressionAttributeValues''','''ConditionExpression=\"#status = :published\",\n            ExpressionAttributeNames={\"#status\": \"status\"},\n            ExpressionAttributeValues''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='tests/test_feed.py'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('''\n\nif __name__''','''\n    def test_hide_removes_from_feed(self):\n        self.lib.publish(\"hello\", \"Hello\", \"...\", \"ann\")\n        self.lib.publish(\"other\", \"Other\", \"...\", \"bob\")\n        self.lib.hide(\"hello\", by=\"ann\")\n        self.assertEqual([s[\"slug\"] for s in self.lib.feed()], [\"other\"])\n        self.assertTrue(self.lib.get(\"hello\")[\"hidden\"])\n\n    def test_hand_hidden_story_stays_out_of_feed(self):\n        # what the AWS CLI write in the staging report produces\n        self.lib.publish(\"hello\", \"Hello\", \"...\", \"ann\")\n        self.lib.table.update_item(\n            Key={\"slug\": \"hello\"}, UpdateExpression=\"SET #h = :t\",\n            ExpressionAttributeNames={\"#h\": \"hidden\"}, ExpressionAttributeValues={\":t\": True})\n        self.assertEqual(self.lib.feed(), [])\n\n    def test_hide_unknown_slug_fails(self):\n        with self.assertRaises(ClientError) as cm:\n            self.lib.hide(\"nope\", by=\"ann\")\n        self.assertEqual(cm.exception.response[\"Error\"][\"Code\"], \"ConditionalCheckFailedException\")\n\n    def test_archive(self):\n        self.lib.publish(\"hello\", \"Hello\", \"...\", \"ann\")\n        self.lib.archive(\"hello\")\n        self.assertEqual(self.lib.get(\"hello\")[\"archived_at\"], self.now)\n\n    def test_no_bare_reserved_words_in_any_expression(self):\n        \"\"\"Guard: every expression the library sends must alias reserved words.\"\"\"\n        from tests.fake_dynamo import RESERVED, _tokens\n        seen = []\n\n        class Spy(FakeTable):\n            def _spy(self, kw):\n                for k in (\"UpdateExpression\", \"ConditionExpression\", \"FilterExpression\", \"ProjectionExpression\"):\n                    if kw.get(k):\n                        seen.append(kw[k])\n            def update_item(self, **kw): self._spy(kw); return super().update_item(**kw)\n            def scan(self, **kw): self._spy(kw); return super().scan(**kw)\n            def put_item(self, **kw): self._spy(kw); return super().put_item(**kw)\n\n        lib = StoryLibrary(Spy(), clock=lambda: 1)\n        lib.publish(\"a\", \"A\", \"b\", \"x\"); lib.rename(\"a\", \"B\"); lib.hide(\"a\", by=\"x\")\n        lib.archive(\"a\"); lib.feed()\n        for expr in seen:\n            toks = _tokens(expr)\n            for i, t in enumerate(toks):\n                if t.upper() in RESERVED and not (i + 1 < len(toks) and toks[i + 1] == \"(\") \\\\\n                        and t.upper() not in {\"SET\", \"AND\", \"OR\", \"NOT\"}:\n                    self.fail(f\"bare reserved word {t!r} in {expr!r}\")\n\n\nif __name__''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nE\ncat > ANSWER.md <<'E'\n# Causes\n\nBoth reports come from the same thing: `hidden` is a DynamoDB **reserved word**, and `src/app.py` used it unescaped.\n\n1. **Prod 500 on hide.** `hide()` wrote `SET hidden = :h, ...`. DynamoDB rejects a bare reserved word in an UpdateExpression with a `ValidationException`, so every hide call failed. Fix: `#hidden` with `ExpressionAttributeNames`.\n\n2. **Staging: hidden story still in the feed.** Dasha's manual write was correct (`hidden: true` was stored). The bug is in the read side. `feed()` used `ProjectionExpression=\"slug, title, hidden, published_at\"`. In a projection, a bare reserved word doesn't raise. The attribute is silently left out of the result. So `i.get(\"hidden\")` was always `None`, the filter kept everything, and the feed returned 200 with no error. It wasn't a cache or a different table. Fix: project `#hidden` through `ExpressionAttributeNames`.\n\n# Related fixes\n\n- `archive()` had the same problem with `status` (reserved) in its ConditionExpression. It would have failed as soon as it was wired up. It now uses `#status`.\n- `feed()` now follows `LastEvaluatedKey`, because a scan returns at most 1 MB per page.\n\n# Keeping it from coming back\n\nAdded tests for hide, for a hand-hidden story (alias write), for hide on an unknown slug, and for archive. Added a guard test that records every expression the library sends and fails if any contains a bare reserved word.\n\nNote that the fake's `RESERVED` list is only a subset of DynamoDB's roughly 570 reserved words. When you add a new attribute name, alias it with `#name` by default.\nE\npython3 -m unittest discover tests 2>&1 | tail -5"}}}
