{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEMSM9NbZp1v2ZKPnYAJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both reports have the same cause: `hidden` is a DynamoDB reserved word, and `src/app.py` used it without an alias. The 10 tests pass, but they run against the in-memory fake, not real DynamoDB. I haven't committed anything.\n\n- **Prod 500 on hide:** `hide()` wrote `SET hidden = :h, ...`. DynamoDB rejects a bare reserved word in an update with a `ValidationException`, so every hide call failed. It now uses a `#hidden` alias.\n- **Staging story still in the feed:** Dasha's manual write was fine, and `hidden: true` was stored. `feed()` listed `hidden` bare in its `ProjectionExpression`. In a projection, DynamoDB doesn't raise an error. It silently drops the attribute. So the `hidden` check never matched, nothing was filtered out, and `/feed` returned 200. It wasn't a cache or a different table. The feed now projects `#hidden` through an alias.\n\nI also fixed two things nearby:\n- **`archive()`:** it had the same bug with `status` in its condition. It isn't wired to the API yet, so it hadn't failed anywhere. It now uses `#status`.\n- **Feed pagination:** `feed()` now follows `LastEvaluatedKey`, since a scan returns at most 1 MB per page.\n\nTo stop it coming back, I added tests for hide, for a story hidden by hand, for hiding an unknown slug, and for `archive`. A guard test records every expression the library sends and fails on any bare reserved word. The fake's `RESERVED` list is only a subset of DynamoDB's roughly 570 words, so the guard won't catch every case. Aliasing new attribute names with `#name` by default is the safer habit.\n\nThe causes are written up in `ANSWER.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2619,"cache_read_input_tokens":27813,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2619},"output_tokens":602,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"05b2b6d4-5f38-481e-928c-27bbdbd78446","uuid":"049a827f-adf2-40f7-9bf6-2f958c73e9e2","timestamp":"2026-10-20T23:25:41.443Z","request_id":"req_011CgEMSLkKhSM2hjv6mHXpf"}
